    q: "What are the key deadlines and timelines in a running-down action?",
    a: "Diary management is critical in PI practice. The key deadlines are:\n\n**Before / on commencement:**\n- **Limitation:** 6 years from the accident (s.6 Limitation Act 1953); **36 months** against a public authority/Government (PAPA / GPA)\n- **Minors/disability:** time does not run until the disability ceases\n- **s.96 RTA notice to insurer:** serve before commencing; strict requirement **within 7 days of issue of the writ**\n- **MIB untraced claims:** police report within **14 days** of the accident\n\n**After service of the writ:**\n- **Memorandum of Appearance:** within **14 days** of service\n- **Statement of Defence:** within **14 days** after appearance / time to file defence\n- **Reply (if any):** within **14 days** of the defence\n\n**Interlocutory / trial:**\n- Notices of Application generally served at least **7 clear days** before hearing\n- Exchange of witness statements and expert reports per case-management directions\n\n**Appeals:**\n- **Notice of Appeal:** within **30 days** of the decision\n- **Memorandum of Appeal:** within **60 days** of the Notice of Appeal\n\n**Practical tip:** Diarise every deadline the moment you take instructions, and set internal reminders well ahead of each date. Many of these periods are strict and non-compliance can be fatal to the claim.\n\n**Caution:** Always verify the current rule text — periods can be revised, and the consolidated ROC 2012 (effective 1 January 2025) should be checked."
